  "review_method": "All 183 fresh native PNG screenshots were visually inspected. The 82 non-call-design images were reviewed in 14 full-resolution contact sheets; the 101 call-design images were independently reviewed in 26 full-resolution sheets. Each source retains its original 480x854 pixels in the sheets. Critical caller-body notification and archive system-bar images were checked explicitly. Native screenshot pixels were not edited; preview montages only arrange originals on labeled canvases.",
  "feature_evidence": {
    "settings_backup_restore": "Three native screenshots show successful file export in both palettes and restore confirmation with counts, preservation explanation, Cancel and Restore. Production SAF intents and real file IO are exercised by instrumentation with a test document provider.",
    "five_launcher_icons": "All five distinct dark-green/gold icon previews and labels are visible across native dialog top/bottom captures in both themes. Scroll-accessible fifth row is fully visible at the bottom. Native tests separately verify enabled launcher aliases.",
    "favorites_strip": "32 contacts/recents presentation variants cover Hebrew/English, light/dark, font1.0/1.3 and compact/expanded states. The strip fits above the list; all favorites are horizontally reachable in native interaction tests.",
    "compact_summary": "48dp compact row and smaller expanded summary show total count/time, outgoing, incoming, missed and average duration without clipped summary content at either font size.",
    "avatar_shapes": "Four distinct clipped shapes appear in actual contact photos/initials and real RemoteViews widget renders. Circle is the default. Native dialogs show all options.",
    "archive_contact_identity": "Both palette captures show the actual temporary Android provider contact name/photo plus secondary number and matching name search. Light archive system clock and navigation icons now have clear dark contrast.",
    "call_notifications": "All six native SystemUI captures show incoming, outgoing and active states, speaker on/off action changes and a clearly visible caller name in the notification body. Full Hebrew and English synthetic contact names fit in the body at font1.3. Native tests acknowledge speaker commands, direct return and hang-up; a real phoneCall foreground service posts the synthetic state.",
    "return_from_call": "Two captures show preserved contacts query/list anchor and settings scroll after native system Back. Native tests cover normal, audio, more and keypad panels without ending the synthetic call."
  },
